WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.140
Man, there's so many memories.

2
00:00:06.140 --> 00:00:20.080
There were times . . . My happiest times was riding horses and going to help with butchers on the weekend.

3
00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:28.040
We'd go pen cows and run cattle.

4
00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:34.860
Everybody had cattle, just about a cow or two, and they would kind of run wild there.

5
00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:38.420
There wasn’t any pound [impoundment] pen laws back then.

6
00:00:38.420 --> 00:00:42.940
And cows was at large and we would go get them and brand them . . .

7
00:00:42.940 --> 00:00:43.140
What's pound pen laws?

8
00:00:42.940 --> 00:00:43.140
. . . in the spring.

9
00:00:42.940 --> 00:00:54.220
You know where . . . they was . . . stock was running at large back on the bayou.

10
00:00:54.220 --> 00:01:01.400
We'd get together and go pen them up.

11
00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:11.900
Uncles and cousins and all had animals, and whoever's cow or calf was on the brand,

12
00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:20.720
they would brand them with that then with the brand that the mama cow had.

13
00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:32.320
It was great to have that kind of freedom and adventure.

14
00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:39.960
They would work you and you'd complain about . . . I had an uncle that ran a farm,

15
00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:48.940
and we would work and my brother, my uncles, and all the boys would work on the farm.

16
00:01:48.940 --> 00:01:54.980
He said, they told us they was educating us about ignorance.

17
00:01:54.980 --> 00:02:07.180
At the time, you know, you’re six, seven years old, you're doing things and you’re really not grasping what they're trying to tell you.

18
00:02:07.180 --> 00:02:16.880
Then later on in life you catch on to what they're saying about educating you about ignorance: that if you don't get a good education,

19
00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:24.640
that you going to have to work hard all your life and you don't want to do that.

20
00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:33.913
Once you realize what they was trying to tell you, you kind of went back to school and stayed on the honor roll.
